-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, 1992 c. 4 -- part ssc5.
-- PART X, CHRISTMAS BONUS FOR PENSIONERS (ss 148 to 150).  Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk (point in time
-- 2026-07-08); it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- Reading a result: JUST FALSE is the Act saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).
-- K3 (s 174, line 4342): in this file "the Administration Act" is the Social Security Administration Act 1992 and "the 1975 Act" is the Social Security Act 1975.
-- Every NOT is bracketed.  Day of the week: Day (a date) MODULO 7 is 0 for Sunday, 1 for Monday ... 6 for Saturday.

§ `Part X -- Christmas bonus for pensioners (ss 148-150)`

§§ `s 150(4) -- the relevant week`

-- The relevant week is the 7 days from the first Monday in December, unless an order names another week.
-- src:3094 | (4) In this Part of this Act “the relevant week”, in relation to any year, means the week beginning with the first Monday in December or such other week as may be specified in an order made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 150(4) (src:3094)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the week an order specifies instead` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A Period
`s 150(4) the relevant week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the week an order specifies instead`
    WHEN JUST other THEN other
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first Monday in December`
            `the last day`  IS `the first Monday in December` PLUS 6
    WHERE
        `the first of December` MEANS Date 1 12 year
        `the first Monday in December` MEANS
            `the first of December` PLUS ((8 MINUS ((Day `the first of December`) MODULO 7)) MODULO 7)

§§ `s 149(1) -- the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man and Gibraltar`

-- Where a person was present or ordinarily resident: the places s 148(1)(a) names, and the three places
-- s 149(1) treats as part of the United Kingdom.  Territorial waters (s 172(b)) are not asked: the person
-- states the place as a fact.
-- src:3006 | (a) is present or ordinarily resident in the United Kingdom , an EEA state or Switzerland at any time during the relevant week; and
@ref s 148(1)(a) (src:3006)
DECLARE `s 148(1)(a) Place` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom`
    `s 148(1)(a) an EEA state`
    `s 148(1)(a) Switzerland`
    `s 149(1) the Channel Islands`
    `s 149(1) the Isle of Man`
    `s 149(1) Gibraltar`
    `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else`

-- src:3023 | (1) For the purposes of section 148 above the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man and Gibraltar shall be treated as though they were part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 149(1) (src:3023)
GIVEN place IS A `s 148(1)(a) Place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 149(1) the Channel Islands` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 149(1) the Isle of Man` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 149(1) Gibraltar` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 149(1) speaks only of the three places
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) an EEA state` THEN NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) Switzerland` THEN NOTHING           -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:3006 | (a) is present or ordinarily resident in the United Kingdom , an EEA state or Switzerland at any time during the relevant week; and
@ref s 148(1)(a) (src:3006)
GIVEN place IS A `s 148(1)(a) Place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) an EEA state` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) Switzerland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 149(1) the Channel Islands` THEN `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` place
    WHEN `s 149(1) the Isle of Man` THEN `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` place
    WHEN `s 149(1) Gibraltar` THEN `s 149(1) the place is treated as part of the United Kingdom` place
    WHEN `s 148(1)(a) somewhere else` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names three places and does not say "only"

§§ `s 148 -- entitlement to the Christmas bonus`

-- A gloss: any person present or ordinarily resident in the UK, an EEA state or Switzerland during the
-- relevant week, who is (or is treated as) entitled to a qualifying benefit for a period that includes a
-- day of that week, is entitled to the bonus for that year, subject to the rest of the Part and to s 1 of
-- the Administration Act (not among the sources: the person states whether it allows the payment).
-- src:3005 | (1) Any person who in any year—
-- src:3006 | (a) is present or ordinarily resident in the United Kingdom , an EEA state or Switzerland at any time during the relevant week; and
-- src:3007 | (b) is entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit in respect of a period which includes a day in that week or is to be treated as entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit in respect of such a period,
-- src:3008 | shall, subject to the following provisions of this Part of this Act and to section 1 of the Administration Act, be entitled to payment under this subsection in respect of that year.
@ref s 148(1) (src:3005-3008)
GIVEN `the place the person was present or ordinarily resident in during the relevant week` IS A `s 148(1)(a) Place`
      `the person is entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit for a period that includes a day in the relevant week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is treated as so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision to which the entitlement is subject allows the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF     `s 124(1) is known to hold` (`s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `the place the person was present or ordinarily resident in during the relevant week`)
       AND (   `the person is entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit for a period that includes a day in the relevant week`
            OR `the person is treated as so entitled`)
       AND `the provision to which the entitlement is subject allows the payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who in any year ... shall ... be entitled"

DECLARE `s 148(2ZA) Provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(1) section 1 of the Administration Act`
    `s 148(2ZA) article 43 of the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`

-- Armed forces independence payment: s 148(1)'s reference to s 1 of the Administration Act is read as a
-- reference to article 43 of the Order.
-- src:3015 | (2ZA) In a case where a person is entitled to a payment of armed forces independence payment, the reference in subsection (1) to section 1 of the Administration Act is to be read as a reference to article 43 of the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011 (S.I. 2011/517).
@ref s 148(2ZA) (src:3015)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a payment of armed forces independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 148(2ZA) Provision`
`s 148(2ZA) the provision to which the entitlement is subject` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to a payment of armed forces independence payment`
    THEN `s 148(2ZA) article 43 of the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`
    ELSE `s 148(1) section 1 of the Administration Act`

-- (2A): in a case within paragraph (c)(ii) of subsection (2), the age in paragraph (a) is the qualifying age for
-- state pension credit instead of pensionable age.
DECLARE `s 148(2A) Age` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(2A) pensionable age`
    `s 148(2A) the qualifying age for state pension credit`

-- src:3016 | (2A) In a case falling within paragraph (c)(ii) of subsection (2) above, paragraph (a) of that subsection has effect with the substitution of “qualifying age for state pension credit” for “pensionable age”.
@ref s 148(2A) (src:3016)
GIVEN `the only qualifying benefit to which the person is entitled is state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 148(2A) Age`
`s 148(2A) the age that paragraph (a) of subsection (2) reads` MEANS
    IF `the only qualifying benefit to which the person is entitled is state pension credit`
    THEN `s 148(2A) the qualifying age for state pension credit`
    ELSE `s 148(2A) pensionable age`

-- A gloss: a member of a couple who is entitled under (1) also gets a payment if both members reached
-- pensionable age by the end of the relevant week, the other member was present or resident in a named
-- place, and either he gets an increase for the other member or his only qualifying benefit is state
-- pension credit.  In the state-pension-credit case (2A) the age in (a) is the qualifying age for it.
-- src:3009 | (2) Subject to the following provisions of this Part of this Act, any person who is a member of a couple and is entitled to a payment under subsection (1) above in respect of a year shall also be entitled to payment under this subsection in respect of that year if—
-- src:3010 | (a) both members have attained pensionable age not later than the end of the relevant week; and
-- src:3011 | (b) the other member satisfies the condition mentioned in subsection (1)(a) above; and
-- src:3012 | (c) either—
-- src:3013 | (i) he is entitled or treated as entitled, in respect of the other member, to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit; or
-- src:3014 | (ii) the only qualifying benefit to which he is entitled is state pension credit.
@ref s 148(2) (src:3009-3014)
GIVEN `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 137(1) the two persons are a couple` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      couple IS A Couple
      `the date the one member attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A DATE
      `the date the other member attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A DATE
      `the place the other member was present or ordinarily resident in during the relevant week` IS A `s 148(1)(a) Place`
      `the last day of the relevant week` IS A DATE
      `the person is entitled or treated as entitled, in respect of the other member, to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only qualifying benefit to which the person is entitled is state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(2) the member of the couple is also entitled to payment under subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 124(1) holds or else nothing` (`s 124(1) both hold` `s 137(1) the two persons are a couple` `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who is a member of a couple and is entitled to a payment under subsection (1)"
    WHEN JUST member THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall also be entitled to payment under this subsection in respect of that year if" -- a failed condition gives JUST FALSE
        `s 124(1) both hold`
            (`s 124(1) both hold` (JUST `paragraph (a) holds`) `paragraph (b) answer`)
            (JUST `paragraph (c) holds`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 148(2A) the age that paragraph (a) of subsection (2) reads` `the only qualifying benefit to which the person is entitled is state pension credit`
            WHEN `s 148(2A) the qualifying age for state pension credit` THEN
                    (`the date the one member attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` AT MOST `the last day of the relevant week`)
                AND (`the date the other member attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` AT MOST `the last day of the relevant week`)
            WHEN `s 148(2A) pensionable age` THEN
                    (couple's `one member`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST `the last day of the relevant week`)
                AND (couple's `the other member`'s `date of attaining pensionable age` AT MOST `the last day of the relevant week`)
        `paragraph (b) answer` MEANS
            `s 148(1)(a) the place is one the paragraph names` `the place the other member was present or ordinarily resident in during the relevant week`
        `paragraph (c) holds` MEANS
            `the person is entitled or treated as entitled, in respect of the other member, to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit`
            OR `the only qualifying benefit to which the person is entitled is state pension credit`

-- The payment is made by the Secretary of State.
-- src:3017 | (3) A payment under subsection (1) or (2) above—
-- src:3018 | (a) is to be made by the Secretary of State; and
@ref s 148(3)(a) (src:3017-3018)
`s 148(3)(a) who makes the payment` MEANS `the Secretary of State`

-- The payment is £10 or a larger sum the Secretary of State specifies by order.  An order that names exactly
-- £10 leaves the payment at £10 (the first limb and the second agree).  An order that names less than £10 is
-- outside what the subsection authorises, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3019 | (b) is to be of £10 or such larger sum as the Secretary of State may by order specify.
@ref s 148(3)(b) (src:3019)
GIVEN `the sum the order specifies, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sum the order specifies, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 10
    WHEN JUST sum THEN
        IF sum AT LEAST 10
        THEN JUST sum
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "£10 or such larger sum as the Secretary of State may by order specify"

-- src:3021 | (5) Only one sum shall be payable in respect of any person.
@ref s 148(5) (src:3021)
GIVEN `a sum has already been paid under section 148 in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(5) a further sum is payable in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `a sum has already been paid under section 148 in respect of the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Only one sum shall be payable in respect of any person."
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not say that a first sum is payable

§§ `s 149 -- provisions supplementary to s 148`

-- A gloss: a person is treated as entitled to a qualifying benefit if the person would be entitled but for
-- the fact that the person or the other member of the couple gets some other payment out of public funds
-- (a benefit other than state pension credit), or, for state pension credit, but for exceptional income.
-- src:3024 | (2) A person shall be treated for the purposes of section 148(1)(b) above as entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit if he would be so entitled—
-- src:3025 | (a) in the case of a qualifying benefit other than state pension credit, but for the fact that he or, if he is a member of a couple, the other member is entitled to receive some other payment out of public funds;
-- src:3026 | (b) in the case of state pension credit, but for the fact that his income or, if he is a member of a couple, the income of the other member was exceptionally of an amount which resulted in his having ceased to be entitled to state pension credit.
@ref s 149(2) (src:3024-3026)
GIVEN `the benefit is state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be entitled but for the fact that the person or the other member of the couple is entitled to receive some other payment out of public funds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be entitled but for the fact that the income of the person or of the other member of the couple was exceptionally of an amount which resulted in the person's ceasing to be entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(2) the person is treated as entitled to a payment of the qualifying benefit` MEANS
    IF     (    (NOT `the benefit is state pension credit`)
            AND `the person would be entitled but for the fact that the person or the other member of the couple is entitled to receive some other payment out of public funds`)
        OR (    `the benefit is state pension credit`
            AND `the person would be entitled but for the fact that the income of the person or of the other member of the couple was exceptionally of an amount which resulted in the person's ceasing to be entitled`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated ... as entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit if he would be so entitled"

-- src:3027 | (3) A person shall be treated for the purposes of section 148(2)(c)(i) above as entitled in respect of the other member of the couple to an increase in a payment of a qualifying benefit if he would be so entitled—
-- src:3028 | (a) but for the fact that he or the other member is entitled to receive some other payment out of public funds;
-- src:3029 | (b) but for the operation of any provision of ... paragraph 6(4) of Schedule 7 to this Act or any regulations made under paragraph 6(3) of that Schedule whereby entitlement to benefit is affected by the amount of a person’s earnings in a given period.
@ref s 149(3) (src:3027-3029)
GIVEN `the person would be entitled to the increase but for the fact that the person or the other member of the couple is entitled to receive some other payment out of public funds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be entitled to the increase but for the operation of a provision whereby entitlement to benefit is affected by the amount of a person's earnings in a given period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(3) the person is treated as entitled to an increase in the payment of the qualifying benefit` MEANS
    IF `the person would be entitled to the increase but for the fact that the person or the other member of the couple is entitled to receive some other payment out of public funds`
       OR `the person would be entitled to the increase but for the operation of a provision whereby entitlement to benefit is affected by the amount of a person's earnings in a given period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated ... as entitled in respect of the other member of the couple to an increase ... if he would be so entitled"

-- src:3030 | (4) For the purposes of section 148 above a person shall be taken not to be entitled to a payment of a war disablement pension unless not later than the end of the relevant week he has attained pensionable age.
@ref s 149(4) (src:3030)
GIVEN `the payment is a war disablement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person attains pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the relevant week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(4) the person is entitled to a payment of the war disablement pension` MEANS
    IF `the payment is a war disablement pension` AND (`the date the person attains pensionable age` GREATER THAN `the last day of the relevant week`)
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be taken not to be entitled to a payment of a war disablement pension unless not later than the end of the relevant week he has attained pensionable age"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only takes a person NOT to be entitled; it does not say when a person is

-- src:3031 | (5) A sum payable under section 148 above shall not be treated as benefit for the purposes of any enactment or instrument under which entitlement to the relevant qualifying benefit arises or is to be treated as arising.
@ref s 149(5) (src:3031)
GIVEN `the sum is payable under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(5) the sum is treated as benefit for the purposes of the enactment or instrument under which entitlement to the qualifying benefit arises` MEANS
    IF `the sum is payable under section 148`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be treated as benefit"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

DECLARE `s 149(6) Purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 149(6) for the purposes of income tax`
    `s 149(6) for the purposes of an enactment or instrument under which regard is had to a person's means`
    `s 149(6) for some other purpose`

-- src:3032 | (6) A payment and the right to receive a payment—
-- src:3033 | (a) under section 148 above or any enactment corresponding to it in Northern Ireland; or
-- src:3034 | (b) under regulations relating to widows which are made by the Secretary of State under any enactment relating to police and which contain a statement that the regulations provide for payments corresponding to payments under that section,
-- src:3035 | shall be disregarded for all purposes of income tax and for the purposes of any enactment or instrument under which regard is had to a person’s means.
@ref s 149(6) (src:3032-3035)
GIVEN `the payment or the right to it is under section 148 or the corresponding enactment in Northern Ireland, or under regulations relating to widows made under an enactment relating to police and containing the statement the paragraph describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 149(6) Purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(6) the payment and the right to receive it are disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the payment or the right to it is under section 148 or the corresponding enactment in Northern Ireland, or under regulations relating to widows made under an enactment relating to police and containing the statement the paragraph describes`
    THEN
        CONSIDER purpose
        WHEN `s 149(6) for the purposes of income tax` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 149(6) for the purposes of an enactment or instrument under which regard is had to a person's means` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 149(6) for some other purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be disregarded for all purposes of income tax and for the purposes of any enactment or instrument under which regard is had to a person's means"
    ELSE NOTHING                                              -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 150 -- interpretation of Part X`

DECLARE `s 150(1) Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(1)(a) a retirement pension`
    `s 150(1)(b) long-term incapacity benefit`
    `s 150(1)(ba) a qualifying employment and support allowance`
    `s 150(1)(bb) personal independence payment`
    `s 150(1)(bc) armed forces independence payment`
    `s 150(1)(bd) adult disability payment`
    `s 150(1)(c) a widowed mother's allowance, widowed parent's allowance or widow's pension`
    `s 150(1)(e) a carer's allowance`
    `s 150(1)(ea) carer support payment`
    `s 150(1)(f) industrial death benefit`
    `s 150(1)(g) an attendance allowance`
    `s 150(1)(h) an unemployability supplement or allowance`
    `s 150(1)(i) a war disablement pension`
    `s 150(1)(j) a war widow's pension`
    `s 150(1)(k) state pension credit`
    `s 150(1)(l) a mobility supplement`
    `s 150(1) a payment of some other kind`

-- src:3037 | (1) In this Part of this Act “qualifying benefit” means—
-- src:3038 | (a) a retirement pension;
-- src:3039 | (b) long-term incapacity benefit;
-- src:3040 | (ba) a qualifying employment and support allowance;
-- src:3041 | (bb) personal independence payment;
-- src:3042 | (bc) armed forces independence payment;
-- src:3043 | (bd) adult disability payment,
-- src:3044 | (c) a widowed mother’s allowance, widowed parent’s allowance or widow’s pension;
-- src:3045 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:3046 | (e) a carer’s allowance;
-- src:3047 | (ea) carer support payment;
-- src:3048 | (f) industrial death benefit;
-- src:3049 | (g) an attendance allowance;
-- src:3050 | (h) an unemployability supplement or allowance;
-- src:3051 | (i) a war disablement pension;
-- src:3052 | (j) a war widow’s pension;
-- src:3053 | (k) state pension credit;
-- src:3054 | (l) a mobility supplement.
@ref s 150(1) (src:3037-3054)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 150(1) Kind of payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 150(1) a payment of some other kind` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying benefit” means—"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 150(2) Kind of retirement pension` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(2) a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014`
    `s 150(2) a retirement pension under this Act`
    `s 150(2) graduated retirement benefit`
    `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of pension`

-- src:3075 | “retirement pension” means—
-- src:3076 | a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014,
-- src:3077 | a retirement pension under this Act, or
-- src:3078 | graduated retirement benefit;
@ref s 150(2) “retirement pension” (src:3075-3078)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 150(2) Kind of retirement pension`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the payment is a retirement pension` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of pension` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“retirement pension” means—"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3074 | “qualifying employment and support allowance” means a contributory allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 the calculation of the amount of which includes an addition in respect of the support component or the work-related activity component;
@ref s 150(2) “qualifying employment and support allowance” (src:3074)
GIVEN `the allowance is a contributory allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the calculation of its amount includes an addition in respect of the support component or the work-related activity component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the allowance is a qualifying employment and support allowance` MEANS
    IF `the allowance is a contributory allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
       AND `the calculation of its amount includes an addition in respect of the support component or the work-related activity component`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying employment and support allowance” means"

-- src:3069 | “mobility supplement” means a supplement awarded in respect of disablement which affects a person’s ability to walk and for which the person is in receipt of war disablement pension;
@ref s 150(2) “mobility supplement” (src:3069)
GIVEN `the supplement was awarded in respect of disablement which affects the person's ability to walk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in receipt of war disablement pension for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the supplement is a mobility supplement` MEANS
    IF `the supplement was awarded in respect of disablement which affects the person's ability to walk`
       AND `the person is in receipt of war disablement pension for it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“mobility supplement” means"

DECLARE `s 150(2) Kind of attendance payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(2) an attendance allowance`
    `s 150(2) a disability living allowance`
    `s 150(2) an increase of disablement pension under section 104 or 105`
    `s 150(2) a payment under regulations made under section 159(3)(b) of the 1975 Act or paragraph 7(2) of Schedule 8`
    `s 150(2) an increase of allowance under Article 8 of the Pneumoconiosis, Byssinosis and Miscellaneous Diseases Benefit Scheme 1983 or a corresponding provision`
    `s 150(2) an allowance in respect of constant attendance for which a person is in receipt of war disablement pension`
    `s 150(2) a child disability payment given under regulations made under section 31 of the Social Security (Scotland) Act 2018`
    `s 150(2) pension age disability payment`
    `s 150(2) Scottish adult disability living allowance`
    `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of attendance payment`

-- Closing words of subsection (2): each of "attendance allowance", "unemployability supplement or allowance",
-- "war disablement pension" and "war widow's pension" includes any payment the Secretary of State accepts as
-- analogous to it.  The list is not closed, so a payment not accepted is NOTHING, never FALSE.
-- src:3092 | and each of the following expressions, namely “attendance allowance”, “unemployability supplement or allowance”, “war disablement pension” and “war widow’s pension”, includes any payment which the Secretary of State accepts as being analogous to it.
@ref s 150(2) (src:3092)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes any payment which the Secretary of State accepts as being analogous to it"

-- "attendance allowance" means the nine listed payments, and (closing words of subsection (2)) includes any
-- payment the Secretary of State accepts as analogous: so a payment of another kind is NOTHING when the
-- Secretary of State has not accepted it, and JUST TRUE when he has.
-- src:3058 | “attendance allowance” means—
-- src:3059 | an attendance allowance;
-- src:3060 | a disability living allowance;
-- src:3061 | an increase of disablement pension under section 104 or 105 above;
-- src:3062 | a payment under regulations made in exercise of the powers in section 159(3)(b) of the 1975 Act or paragraph 7(2) of Schedule 8 to this Act;
-- src:3063 | an increase of allowance under Article 8 of the Pneumoconiosis, Byssinosis and Miscellaneous Diseases Benefit Scheme 1983 (constant attendance allowance for certain persons to whom that Scheme applies) or under the corresponding provision of any Scheme which may replace that Scheme;
-- src:3064 | an allowance in respect of constant attendance on account of disablement for which a person is in receipt of war disablement pension, including an allowance in respect of exceptionally severe disablement;
-- src:3065 | a child disability payment given in accordance with regulations made under section 31 of the Social Security (Scotland) Act 2018 (asp 9);
-- src:3066 | pension age disability payment given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024;
-- src:3067 | Scottish adult disability living allowance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
@ref s 150(2) “attendance allowance” (src:3058-3067)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 150(2) Kind of attendance payment`
      `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to an attendance allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the payment is an attendance allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of attendance payment` THEN
        `s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to an attendance allowance`
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 150(2) Kind of unemployability payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(2) an unemployability supplement payable under Part I of Schedule 7`
    `s 150(2) a corresponding allowance payable by virtue of paragraph 6(4)(a) of Schedule 8`
    `s 150(2) a corresponding supplement to retired pay or pension exempt from income tax under section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`
    `s 150(2) a corresponding allowance under the Personal Injuries (Emergency Provisions) Act 1939`
    `s 150(2) a corresponding supplement to retired pay or pension under the Polish Resettlement Act 1947`
    `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of unemployability payment`

-- src:3080 | “unemployability supplement or allowance” means—
-- src:3081 | an unemployability supplement payable under Part I of Schedule 7 to this Act; or
-- src:3082 | any corresponding allowance payable—
-- src:3083 | by virtue of paragraph 6(4)(a) of Schedule 8 to this Act;
-- src:3084 | by way of supplement to retired pay or pension exempt from income tax under section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003;
-- src:3085 | under the Personal Injuries (Emergency Provisions) Act 1939; ...
-- src:3086 | by way of supplement to retired pay or pension under the Polish Resettlement Act 1947; or
@ref s 150(2) “unemployability supplement or allowance” (src:3080-3086)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 150(2) Kind of unemployability payment`
      `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to an unemployability supplement or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the payment is an unemployability supplement or allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of unemployability payment` THEN
        `s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to an unemployability supplement or allowance`
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 150(2) Kind of war disablement pension` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(2) retired pay, pension or allowance granted in respect of disablement under a listed Act`
    `s 150(2) retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies`
    `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war disablement pension`

-- src:3088 | “war disablement pension” means—
-- src:3089 | any retired pay, pension or allowance granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under the Air Force (Constitution) Act 1917, the Personal Injuries (Emergency Provisions) Act 1939, the Pensions (Navy, Army, Air Force and Mercantile Marine) Act 1939, the Polish Resettlement Act 1947, or Part VII or section 151 of the Reserve Forces Act 1980;
-- src:3090 | without prejudice to paragraph (a) of this definition, any retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies;
@ref s 150(2) “war disablement pension” (src:3088-3090)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 150(2) Kind of war disablement pension`
      `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to a war disablement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the payment is a war disablement pension` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war disablement pension` THEN
        `s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to a war disablement pension`
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 150(2) Kind of war widow's pension` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(2) a widow's or surviving civil partner's pension or allowance granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable under an enactment mentioned in the definition of war disablement pension`
    `s 150(2) a pension or allowance for a widow or surviving civil partner granted under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`
    `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war widow's pension`

-- src:3091 | “war widow’s pension” means any widow’s or surviving civil partner's pension or allowance granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable by virtue of any enactment mentioned in paragraph (a) of the preceding definition or a pension or allowance for a widow or surviving civil partner granted under any scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003;
@ref s 150(2) “war widow’s pension” (src:3091)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 150(2) Kind of war widow's pension`
      `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to a war widow's pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the payment is a war widow's pension` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 150(2) a payment of some other kind of war widow's pension` THEN
        `s 150(2) the payment is included because the Secretary of State accepts it as analogous` `the Secretary of State accepts the payment as analogous to a war widow's pension`
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 150(2) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 150(2) adult disability payment`
    `s 150(2) armed forces independence payment`
    `s 150(2) carer support payment`
    `s 150(2) pensionable age`
    `s 150(2) state pension credit`

-- The terms of subsection (2) that are fixed by another Act or instrument: one record each (the Act points at the
-- instrument and the encoding does not restate it), and a table that finds the record.  The terms that are tests
-- on facts have a function above; "qualifying age for state pension credit" is s 137(1)'s, repeated word for word.
-- src:3056 | “adult disability payment” means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022,
@ref s 150(2) “adult disability payment” (src:3056)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 150(2) adult disability payment` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022"

-- src:3057 | “armed forces independence payment” means armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011 (S.I. 2011/517);
@ref s 150(2) “armed forces independence payment” (src:3057)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 150(2) armed forces independence payment` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011 (S.I. 2011/517)"

-- src:3068 | “carer support payment” means the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023;
@ref s 150(2) “carer support payment” (src:3068)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 150(2) carer support payment` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023"

-- src:3070 | “pensionable age” has the meaning given by the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995;
@ref s 150(2) “pensionable age” (src:3070)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 150(2) pensionable age` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
        `what it points at or says` IS "the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995"

-- src:3079 | “state pension credit” means state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002;
@ref s 150(2) “state pension credit” (src:3079)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 150(2) state pension credit` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002"

GIVEN term IS A `s 150(2) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 150(2) how the term is defined` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 150(2) adult disability payment` THEN `s 150(2) adult disability payment`
    WHEN `s 150(2) armed forces independence payment` THEN `s 150(2) armed forces independence payment`
    WHEN `s 150(2) carer support payment` THEN `s 150(2) carer support payment`
    WHEN `s 150(2) pensionable age` THEN `s 150(2) pensionable age`
    WHEN `s 150(2) state pension credit` THEN `s 150(2) state pension credit`

-- src:3071 | “the qualifying age for state pension credit” is (in accordance with section 1(2)(b) and (6) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002)—
-- src:3072 | in the case of a woman, pensionable age; or
-- src:3073 | in the case of a man, the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day as the man;
@ref s 150(2) “the qualifying age for state pension credit” (src:3071-3073)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the date a woman born on the same day as the man would attain pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 150(2) the date the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` MEANS
    `s 137(1) the date the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` person `the date a woman born on the same day as the man would attain pensionable age`

-- "couple" in this Part has the meaning in s 137(1).
-- src:3093 | (3) In this Part of this Act, “couple” has the meaning given by section 137(1) above.
@ref s 150(3) (src:3093)
GIVEN couple IS A Couple
      `the circumstances are ones prescribed to take the pair out of limb two` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(3) the two persons are a couple` MEANS
    `s 137(1) the two persons are a couple` couple `the circumstances are ones prescribed to take the pair out of limb two`
